{{Quote|The oviparous quadruped is found on the desert planet of Arvala-7, where it makes its home in the caves that line the desert's rocky ranges. Here it builds its nest and tends to its young.|Ardis San Tekka, in her journal|<ref name="Bestiary">''[[Star Wars Bestiary, Vol. 1: Creatures of the Galaxy]]''</ref>}}
The '''mudhorn cave''' was located on the [[desert]] [[planet]] [[Arvala-7]]. In [[9 ABY]], the [[bounty hunter]] [[Din Djarin]] stole a [[mudhorn egg]] from a [[mudhorn]] living in the [[cave]], managing to [[Death|defeat]] the creature with the help of the [[Force-sensitive]] [[Youngling|child]] [[Din Grogu|Grogu]].

==Description==
The mudhorn cave was located on the [[desert]] [[planet]] [[Arvala-7]],<ref name="Handbook" /> nestled in a crater<ref name="PostGCW">{{EncyclopediaCite|Post-Galactic Civil War and the Mandalorian}}</ref> within one of the world's [[Stone|rocky]] ranges.<ref name="Handbook" /> Featuring striated walls,<ref name="Audio Description">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 2: The Child}} {{AD|Disney+}}</ref> the [[cave]]'s interior was cool, dark,<ref name="Mudhorn DB">{{Databank|mudhorn|mudhorn}}</ref> and muddy, with [[bone]]s strewn across the surface.<ref name="Chapter 2" />

==History==
[[File:MudhornExitsCave-TheChild.png|thumb|300px|left|Djarin watches the mudhorn exit its cave.]]
By the time of the [[New Republic]], a [[mudhorn]], a large horned creature, resided with its [[Mudhorn egg|egg]]<ref name="Chapter 2">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 2: The Child}}</ref>&mdash;called a "sooga"<ref name="PostGCW" /> in the [[Jawaese]] [[language]]<ref name="Chapter 2" />&mdash;in the cave.<ref name="PostGCW" /> In [[9 ABY]],<ref name="Date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of [[The Mandalorian Season One|''The Mandalorian'' Season One]] to [[9 ABY]].</ref> the [[Mandalorian]] [[bounty hunter]]<ref name="Chapter 2" /> [[Din Djarin]]<ref name="PostGCW" /> was taken to the cave by a [[Chettkap's tribe|tribe]] of [[Jawa]]s so he could retrieve the mudhorn's [[egg]]. Djarin entered the cave and soon began fighting the mudhorn when it knocked him out of the cave. Djarin eventually [[Death|killed]] the creature with the help of the [[Force-sensitive]] [[Youngling|child]]<ref name="Chapter 2" /> [[Din Grogu|Grogu]]<ref name="PostGCW" /> and secured the egg, taking it to the Jawas.<ref name="Chapter 2" />

At some point no earlier than [[35 ABY]],<ref name="BestiaryDate">{{BestiaryVol1Date}}</ref> [[Galactic Society of Creature Enthusiasts]]' [[Director of Creature Cartography]], [[Ardis San Tekka]], visited Arvala-7 to study mudhorns. After compiling several drawings of the mudhorn in the mudhorn cave and the surrounding area, she included her observations and the illustrations in her [[Ardis San Tekka's journal|journal]].<ref name="Bestiary" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|At one point there was a big old tree right above the entrance to the mudhorn cave.|Dave Filoni|<ref name="Art of Mandalorian S1">[[The Art of Star Wars: The Mandalorian (Season One)|''The Art of Star Wars: The Mandalorian'' Season One]]</ref>}}	
The mudhorn cave first appeared in "[[Chapter 2: The Child]],"<ref name="Chapter 2" /> the second episode of the [[The Mandalorian Season One|first season]] of the [[Disney+]] live-action series ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]''. The episode aired on [[November 15]], 2019.<ref name="Insider201">{{InsiderCite|201|Star Wars: The Mandalorian Season One Companion|''Star Wars: The Mandalorian'' Season One Companion}}</ref> Prior to the episode's release, the cave appeared in a trailer for the season that was released on [[October 28]], [[2019]], on the official ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[Wikipedia:YouTube|YouTube]] channel.<ref name="Trailer">{{SWYouTube|XmI7WKrAtqs|The Mandalorian &ndash; Official Trailer 2 &#124; Disney+ &#124; Streaming Nov. 12|sw_url=video/trailer-2-the-mandalorian}}</ref> The location received its name in the [[2020]] edition of the [[Monopoly: Star Wars The Mandalorian Edition (2020)|''Monopoly: Star Wars The Mandalorian Edition'']] board game<ref name="Monopoly">[[Monopoly: Star Wars The Mandalorian Edition (2020)|''Monopoly: Star Wars The Mandalorian Edition'' (2020)]]</ref> released on [[September 19]] of that year.<ref name="Amazon">{{Amazon|url=Monopoly-Mandalorian-Protect-Imperial-Enemies/dp/B0884D362F|text=MONOPOLY: Star Wars The Mandalorian Edition Board Game}}</ref> The audio description for the episode suggests that the cave was man-made.<ref name="Audio Description" /> The episode was filmed between [[November 30]] and [[December 13]], [[2018]].<ref name="Art of Mandalorian S1" />

[[File:Mudhorn-Cave-Concept-JamaJurabaev.jpg|thumb|right|300px|Concept art of the cave by Jama Jurabaev]]
Concept art of the cave was drawn by artists [[Christian Alzmann]], [[John Park]], and [[Jama Jurabaev]]. Storyboards were created by [[Dave Lowery]], [[Phillip Norwood]], and [[David Duncan]]. According to series director [[Dave Filoni]], who shot the scene of Djarin entering the cave, the cave at one point had a [[tree]] on top of the entrance,<ref name="Art of Mandalorian S1" /> but this was removed in the final cut of the episode.<ref name="Chapter 2" /> The scene, however, remained unchanged from the early storyboards, as Famuyiwa fully agreed with Filoni's plan.<ref name="Art of Mandalorian S1" />

On [[November 16]], 2020,<ref name="Minecraft DLC">{{SW|url=news/minecraft-star-wars-dlc|text=The ''Minecraft Star Wars'' DLC is the Way}}</ref> the cave was added to the video game ''[[Minecraft]]'' as part of the ''[[Minecraft Star Wars]]'' expansion pack, located on the Arvala-7 section of the map. Within the cave, the player can fight a mudhorn and acquire its egg.<ref name="Minecraft">''[[Minecraft Star Wars]]''</ref> On [[December 16]], 2020,<ref name="Beskar Mando Date">{{ThisWeek|VSRBvBhqGVY|Exciting Lucasfilm Announcements, A New Story From The High Republic, and More!|sw_url=video/exciting-lucasfilm-announcements-a-new-story-from-the-high-republic-and-more}}</ref> the location was added to the mobile game ''[[Star Wars: Galaxy of Heroes]]'' as part of a Hero's Journey event for Din Djarin in his full [[beskar]] [[armor]]. In the game, the cave appears in the second level, in which the player takes control of Djarin to defeat the mudhorn outside.<ref name="Galaxy Heroes">''[[Star Wars: Galaxy of Heroes]]''</ref>

